  "before_claim": "## Statement\n\nAll chart-partition constructions give the same measure $\\mu_r$. Moreover, if $E$ is Borel and contained in any chart $x:U\\to x(U)$, then\n$$\\mu_r(E)=\\int_{x(E)}r_x\\,d\\lambda_n.$$",
  "current_claim": "## Statement\n\nAssume countable choice $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$. For every nonnegative Borel density $r$, chart-partition gluing data as in [[def-countable-chart-gluing-of-a-nonnegative-density-measure]] exist, and all such constructions give the same Borel measure $\\mu_r$. Moreover, if $E$ is Borel and contained in any chart $x:U\\to x(U)$, then\n$$\\mu_r(E)=\\int_{x(E)}r_x\\,d\\lambda_n.$$",
  "changed_clause": "Explicit Countable Choice AC_omega; density independence also states existence of gluing data and the intrinsic measure.",
  "invalidated_claim": "Unqualified use of AC_omega-dependent Borel overlap substitution and/or global gluing existence.",
